diff --git a/extensions/sf-pi-manager/README.md b/extensions/sf-pi-manager/README.md
index da90646f..b25434af 100644
--- a/extensions/sf-pi-manager/README.md
+++ b/extensions/sf-pi-manager/README.md
@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@ open human-facing detail pages, edit low-risk settings, run diagnostics, manage
 recommended packages and external skill roots, and enable or disable bundled
 extensions through Pi's native package filters.
 
+Independently installed extensions can contribute their own Manager row,
+detail page, settings, status, and actions through versioned local discovery.
+Their preferences and lifecycle remain owned by the contributor. External rows
+do not affect bundled counts, package filters, or enable-all/disable-all.
+
 The Manager is always active. Extension state changes update `settings.json` and
 reload Pi because package filters are evaluated at startup.
 
@@ -31,6 +36,35 @@ Common commands are:
 The Manager detail page is the primary no-args destination for bundled extension
 commands. Explicit subcommands remain direct and scriptable.
 
+## External extension contributions
+
+Manager emits `sf-pi-manager:external-extensions` synchronously with
+`{ version: 1, cwd, scope, extensions: [] }`. A loaded contributor that supports
+version 1 may append a cached descriptor with `id`, `name`, `description`,
+`category`, `enabled`, and optional `maturity`, `commands`, `tools`, `events`,
+`statusLines`, `getConfigPanel`, and `setEnabled` fields. Discovery must not load
+models, perform network calls, or start subprocesses. Manager accepts at most 32
+descriptors, validates bounded display fields, and rejects bundled ID collisions
+and the command scope keywords `global` and `project`;
+the first accepted external descriptor wins a duplicate ID.
+
+`getConfigPanel` returns the existing async ConfigPanelFactory contract:
+`(theme, cwd, scope, done, tui?, ctx?) => Focusable`. The panel also implements
+Component; Manager supplies the border and optional scroll handling. A panel
+calls `done(undefined)` when finished, or `done({ needsReload: true })` when a Pi
+reload is required. `setEnabled(enabled, ctx, scope)` saves the contributor's
+own global/project preference and applies its lifecycle change. Manager does
+not write contributor preferences or add contributor paths to SF Pi filters.
+
+External extensions reuse `sf-pi-manager:actions` for action discovery and
+`sf-pi-manager:open` for interactive detail/settings deep links. Their IDs are
+available in `/sf-pi open`, targeted enable/disable completion, and list/status
+even when SF Pi has no package-filter entry in the selected scope. Settings
+scope changes and completed actions refresh cached external descriptors.
+
+See `lib/external-extensions.ts` for the structural wire types. Contributors can
+implement these event payloads without importing SF Pi implementation modules.
+
 ## Configuration
 
 Manager-owned settings include package filters, shared display profile, privacy
@@ -53,6 +87,8 @@ versions.
 ## Safety and Data Boundaries
 
 - Only SF Pi Manager writes the package-filter enable/disable state.
+- External contributions own their preferences; bundled bulk actions never
+  invoke their enablement callbacks or inspect paths in their packages.
 - Native Auto Update is opt-in, interactive-only, abortable, output-redacted,
   and bounded to eligible unpinned npm packages plus the Salesforce CLI step.
 - Pinned, local, Git, project-scoped, incompatible, and unverifiable packages
